  "semantics": [
    "Sound initialization calls the identified CDialog base,sets page/volume captions,then reads each live config BYTE and uses the actual toggle method to set normalized BOOL fields and exact ON/OFF labels. It ignores the base return and returns literalTRUE.",
    "Both sound/music toggles test the entire32-bit BOOL for zero and write0or1. XOR1 is not equivalent for values2/128/high bits.",
    "The slider range is0..16383 with redrawTRUE in both actual MFC range messages;position is16383-configDWORDvolume and tick frequency2048. The range helper rereads HWND between its two SendMessage calls;caller position/tick messages also consume live HWNDs.",
    "Sound OnOK stores lowBYTEs of both32-bit fields before querying slider position,then stores DWORD16383-position and executes the actual no-op CPropertyPage::OnOK. No extra boolean normalization or volume clamp added.",
    "Gameplay initialization uses lowBYTEdifficulty from the observed DWORD view and a fullDWORD lives value. It decrements each working selector before invoking the actual cycle method,then rereads the full title-menu guard independently for two EnableWindow and two ShowWindow calls.",
    "Difficulty cycles0..2 with Beginner/Medium/Herculean labels. Lives cycles2..4 with Two/Three/Four Lives labels. Signed upper-bound checks are preserved;no invented lower-bound clamp.",
    "Only nonzero title-menu guard enables the two selector buttons;the two explanatory labels use SW_HIDE0 when enabled and SW_SHOWNA8 otherwise. Each call sees later callback mutations rather than an entry snapshot.",
    "Gameplay OnOK stores only the low difficulty BYTE and the full lives DWORD before the actual base no-op. Other registry bytes remain owned and unchanged except explicitly modeled endpoint effects."
  ],
